:name: EX-F02 - key extraction
:description: COMM, OBC and EPS on a CAN hub. The attacker is on the space link, asking for a memory dump

# Execution profile (design 4.3; rules G1/G2 of section 9.2). Renode's Monitor has no conditionals,
# so the profile is a file the harness swaps by overriding $profile - the same mechanism $injector
# uses, and for the same reason: a relative include inside an included file resolves against
# Renode's own working directory, not this file.
#
# This include is FIRST on purpose. A failing command aborts the rest of a .resc file, so a profile
# that cannot be found takes the machines down with it and the failure is loud. Last, it would have
# been silent in the worst way: every node built, running with no quantum set at all.
$profile?=@~/space-cs-sim/scripts/profiles/interactive.resc
include $profile

# Every path below hangs off $out, and $out has NO default on purpose - EX-F01's scenario says why
# at length. Unset, LoadELF fails where you can see it, which beats booting another checkout's
# firmware. The harness always passes it; for a manual run, so must you:
#
#   renode -e '$out=@'"$(make -s out)" -e 'include @<this file>' -e start
#
# The OBC is the F02 pair's vulnerable half by default: report signing ON, which is what puts the
# SDLS key in its flash, and EX-F01's length check ON, so the overflow is not a second way in. The
# verifier overrides $obc with the hardened half.
$comm?=$out/build-comm/zephyr/zephyr.elf
$obc?=$out/build-obc-f02-vuln/zephyr/zephyr.elf
$eps?=$out/build-eps-hard/zephyr/zephyr.elf
$commuart?=$out/f02-comm.uart
$obcuart?=$out/f02-obc.uart
$epsuart?=$out/f02-eps.uart
$linkport?=3777

emulation CreateCANHub "canHub"

# The plain radio, as in EX-F01. It frames whatever the OBC sends it, a dump report included.
mach create "COMM"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub
sysbus LoadELF $comm
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $commuart true
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $linkport "spacelink" false
connector Connect sysbus.usart2 spacelink
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1

mach create "OBC"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub
sysbus LoadELF $obc
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $obcuart true
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1

# The EPS is EX-F01's: present and hardened, so the spacecraft around the target is the one EX-F01
# attacked and only the OBC has changed. It is not a target here and nothing in EX-F02 talks to it.
mach create "EPS"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub
sysbus LoadELF $eps
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $epsuart true
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1
# No attacker machine and no CAN injector. The attacker holds a radio, as in EX-F01: everything it
# sends is a telecommand the ground station could have sent, on the operator's own space link.
